Use portable crypto implementations on PS5's execute-only code mappings.

Nettle's SHA-256 assembly reads its shuffle mask from .text, and GnuTLS's
accelerated SHA-512 reads round constants from .text. Both cause native
SYSTEM_XO_VIOLATION faults during HTTPS playback. Disable these dependencies'
assembly/acceleration through their supported configure switches. TLS and
certificate verification remain enabled; FFmpeg codec optimizations are
unaffected.

Upstream: PS5-only; this patch series is not applied on other platforms.

--- a/depends/common/nettle/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/depends/common/nettle/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -44,6 +44,7 @@
                       --enable-static
                       --disable-shared
                       --disable-openssl
+                      --disable-assembler
                       --disable-documentation
                       --enable-pic
                       ${nettle_conf}
--- a/depends/common/gnutls/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/depends/common/gnutls/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -52,6 +52,7 @@
                       --prefix=${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}
                       --enable-static
                       --disable-shared
+                      --disable-hardware-acceleration
                       --without-p11-kit
                       --without-idn
                       --disable-nls
